2246932983]]}, {"t": " go", "lp": -0.007888354361057281, "top": [[" go", -0.007888354361057281], [" install", -4.9748454093933105]]}, {"t": " in", "lp": -0.22721999883651733, "top": [[" in", -0.22721999883651733], [" to", -1.6495260000228882]]}, {"t": " `/", "lp": -0.0020173857919871807, "top": [[" `/", -0.0020173857919871807], [" `", -6.575042247772217]]}, {"t": "usr", "lp": -7.522389205405489e-05, "top": [["usr", -7.522389205405489e-05], [" usr", -10.684260368347168]]}, {"t": "/lib", "lp": -0.000592168653383851, "top": [["/lib", -0.000592168653383851], ["`", -9.897631645202637]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.0097190635278821, "top": [["`", -0.0097190635278821], ["`,", -4.7286577224731445]]}, {"t": " (", "lp": -0.08350158482789993, "top": [[" (", -0.08350158482789993], ["\n\n", -2.5629003047943115]]}, {"t": "not", "lp": -0.36593031883239746, "top": [["not", -0.36593031883239746], ["av", -2.3298280239105225]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, not the default GCC.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into confusing errors.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp`** \u2014 Source directory (where the git repo was checked out)\n- **`-B \"${srcdir}/build`** \u2014 Build directory (where compilation artifacts go)\n- **`-G Ninja`** \u2014 Use the Ninja build system (fast, efficient generator) instead of Make\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimize for performance (enables `-O3`-style optimizations). This is critical for an inference engine.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`** \u2014 Where `make install` will place files\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib`** \u2014 Libraries go in `/usr/lib` (not"}